A||||7||billfredmike24||Removing bolts when doing sunroof swap?||||1||
Z||000000||billfredmike24||08-03-2001||01:09 PM||||I've got all the pieces out of the interior of my donor car and was trying to get the bolts out that hold the skin to the the frame.  I got two of the six bolts out and also the two nuts off from the front  corners.  My problem is the other four bolts will turn, but will not come out any.  I'm thinking that possibly the part that the bolt screws into, that is attached to the roof skin, broke.  Any ideas on what i can do, has anyone had this problem before.  I've searched for a couple hours on the forum and have come up with nothing. Help please, Mike<p>[This message has been edited by billfredmike24 (edited 08-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||88CoupeV6||08-03-2001||02:00 PM||||I've never heard of that happening. all mine came out fine when I did the swap.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> sorry I am not any help.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">   <BR><B>Also 88 Yellow GT</B> :D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||9
