Z||000005||88CoupeV6||08-05-2001||08:39 AM||||I don't know how to fix the bolts, but to fix a crack in the a pillar I would use this stuff you can get at autozone. It is a 2 part epoxy. It worked great on my bumper. I used it all over the car on any imperfections before it went to the paint shop. It had a 2 inch bumper tear. I also filled the holes for the Word pontiac I removed.<BR>Here is a pic.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fbr.jpg">   <P>Good luck<P><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">   <BR><B>Also 88 Yellow GT</B> :D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||billfredmike24||08-05-2001||01:02 PM||||Thanks for the info Josh.<BR>Anyone know what i can do about the roof???<BR>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000007||mbramble||08-05-2001||05:42 PM||||The roof skin has four pieces of 'channel' that are riveted in and that hold the weatherstripping.  Each of theses pieces of channel have "nuts" built in that the bolts attach to, from inside the car, to hold the roof skin on.  <P>I'm not sure what has happened to your roof skin but is sounds as if some of these "nuts" have broken loose from the channel pieces??  If so, I have made repairs in two different ways.  1. Go to the junkyard and see if you can find a sunroof car that you can remove the channels from.  They are just riveted to the skin; drill out the rivets, remove the bolts from the inside and pull the channels off the car.  The you can just rivet them to your sunroof skin.  2. Take one of the bolts to a hardware store and get some T-nuts that fit it.  Then just drill out the old channel "nut" so that the hole is big enough for the T-nut to fit down thru.  Put a bit of silicone in the hole before you put the T-nut in and then cover the top side of the T-nut/bolt with silicon once you screw the bolts in from the inside of the car.  It will all be covered up once you put the weatherstripping back into place.<p>[This message has been edited by mbramble (edited 08-05-2001).]||||reg||1
